{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/3/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/3`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/3/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：每个矩形对象沿其内部标记像素指示的方向平移，平移距离等于该矩形在垂直于移动方向上的尺寸。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为black。\n  - 网格中有若干个互相分离的单色矩形对象（可以是正方形或长方形），每个矩形对象由同一种非背景色填充。\n  - 每个矩形对象的某一条边的中点位置上有一个不同颜色的标记像素（例如red），该标记像素位于矩形对象内部、紧贴某条边的中央。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 标记像素所贴近的那条边决定了移动方向：标记贴在左边则向左移动，贴在右边则向右移动，贴在上边则向上移动，贴在下边则向下移动。\n  - 移动距离等于矩形在垂直于移动方向上的尺寸（即：若向左移动，距离等于矩形的高度；若向上移动，距离等于矩形的宽度）。\n  - 将整个矩形对象（含标记像素）沿该方向平移该距离。超出网格边界的像素被裁剪。原位置清除为背景色。\n- `Key insight`：标记像素的位置编码了移动方向，而移动距离并非直接可读，而是取决于矩形在正交方向上的尺寸——解题者需要先从标记位置推断方向，再从对象自身的几何形状推导出位移量。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/8a6d367c, eval/332f06d7, eval/a6f40cea, eval/e87109e9, train/57edb29d, train/278e5215, eval/9385bd28, eval/247ef758\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4265\nmechanism=0.5342\nlexical=0.0159\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:sprite, object:square, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:translate, output:crop, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8a6d367c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8a6d367c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"upper colored template mask s\",\n  \"dst\": \"rectangular frame interior d containing partial fill-color seed pixels\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"block-scaled s contains all seed pixels in d\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear dst to bg and paint the full matched scaled mask with the seed color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to the rectangular frame\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3857\nmechanism=0.4347\nlexical=0.0220\ncode_feature=0.7143\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:output_resize, object:marker, object:square, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, operation:translate, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a6f40cea\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3859\nmechanism=0.4620\nlexical=0.0158\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:counter, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:bfs_distance, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:translate, output:crop, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a6f40cea.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a6f40cea.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete partial paths inside a framed rectangle by projecting external color traces inward.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg, a 1px rectangular frame (border color) with uniform interior fill.\n- Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.\n\nRule:\n- Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.\n- Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.\n- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\n- Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.\n\nKey insight: Endpoint colors of two-color traces anchor the alternating phase deterministically.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\